WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:18.022
As everyone crowded near the door to the tower, Zann glanced back.

2
00:00:18.863 --> 00:00:23.566
Mouth wide open, the Beast thrust its giant head toward them.

3
00:00:23.646 --> 00:00:28.309
Crash! The Beast howled with pain and frustration as it hit an invisible barrier.

4
00:00:28.329 --> 00:00:29.850
"I knew it!"

5
00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:30.771
Zann exclaimed.

6
00:00:30.791 --> 00:00:32.292
"It's a Shield spell!"

7
00:00:33.196 --> 00:00:35.217
"What?" Perda sounded confused.

8
00:00:35.237 --> 00:00:37.137
"But we passed straight through it."

9
00:00:37.157 --> 00:00:42.379
"The Shield must have been designed to only keep out the Beast," said Venna.

10
00:00:43.259 --> 00:00:45.579
"Nice thinking, boy," Wyssa added.

11
00:00:45.599 --> 00:00:48.640
"But how did you know the Shield was there?"

12
00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:49.921
Darb asked Zann.

13
00:00:49.941 --> 00:00:55.022
"I figured Morb wouldn't build his lair here if he didn't have a way to keep the Beast

14
00:00:55.162 --> 00:00:56.242
out," Zann explained.

15
00:00:56.262 --> 00:00:59.523
"But the mibbit Perda gestured toward Darb.

16
00:00:59.543 --> 00:01:01.604
"I know," Zann said.

17
00:01:01.624 --> 00:01:07.985
"I figured, or at least I hoped, that Morb had a backup plan, just in case the mibbit

18
00:01:08.045 --> 00:01:09.326
couldn't hold back the Beast."

19
00:01:10.026 --> 00:01:10.906
"That makes sense."

20
00:01:11.146 --> 00:01:12.367
Darb stroked the mibbit.

21
00:01:12.387 --> 00:01:17.188
"If I had a monster like that outside my front door, I'd have a backup plan too!"

22
00:01:17.908 --> 00:01:20.109
The Beast let out another howl of fury.

23
00:01:20.709 --> 00:01:22.149
Gliss shot it a nervous look.

24
00:01:22.489 --> 00:01:23.510
"What do we do now?"

25
00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:24.310
she asked.

26
00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:27.231
"We go in," said Wyssa.

27
00:01:27.251 --> 00:01:32.372
"Carefully." Touching the lock on the door, she muttered a few words.

28
00:01:33.088 --> 00:01:34.388
The door opened with a pop.

29
00:01:35.009 --> 00:01:38.710
With Wyssa in the lead, the group stepped quietly into the tower.

30
00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:44.871
The entryway inside was long and narrow, lit by a procession of flickering wall torches.

31
00:01:44.891 --> 00:01:47.532
"Weird." Perda peered ahead.

32
00:01:47.552 --> 00:01:52.393
"This place looks a lot bigger on the inside than it did from the outside."

33
00:01:52.413 --> 00:01:57.155
"No kidding," Zann said, glancing through an arched doorway.

34
00:01:57.835 --> 00:02:01.736
Beyond was a room so enormous that he couldn't see the far wall.

35
00:02:02.464 --> 00:02:04.225
Gliss was staring through another arch.

36
00:02:04.245 --> 00:02:07.428
"How are we going to find Morb in this place?"

37
00:02:07.448 --> 00:02:09.229
"Or my parents."

38
00:02:09.609 --> 00:02:10.590
Zann looked at Wyssa.

39
00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:12.851
"Are there any spells we could use?"

40
00:02:12.871 --> 00:02:15.813
"Hundreds," she replied.

41
00:02:15.833 --> 00:02:19.876
"But I'm sure Morb has magic sensors in place.

42
00:02:20.677 --> 00:02:24.699
It's better if he doesn't know we're here until we find him."

43
00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:26.961
Suddenly Darb gasped.

44
00:02:26.981 --> 00:02:27.962
"Look out!"

45
00:02:28.722 --> 00:02:30.624
Something burst out of a nearby doorway.

46
00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:35.002
"Uh-oh, it's one of those blob monsters," Zann exclaimed.

47
00:02:35.022 --> 00:02:39.064
"Like the one Morb had guarding the palace back in First City!"

48
00:02:39.084 --> 00:02:42.346
"A sweller from Ductilan."

49
00:02:42.586 --> 00:02:43.287
Wyssa nodded.

50
00:02:43.307 --> 00:02:47.109
"They make crude but effective guards.

51
00:02:47.789 --> 00:02:49.750
Fortunately they aren't very smart."

52
00:02:50.510 --> 00:02:54.853
She pulled a handful of stones out of her pocket and tossed them down a side hallway.

53
00:02:55.533 --> 00:02:57.134
The sweller blobbed after them.

54
00:02:57.154 --> 00:03:00.376
"This way," Wyssa said, heading down a different hall.

55
00:03:01.128 --> 00:03:03.370
Zann peered into each room they passed.

56
00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:05.671
No two looked the same.

57
00:03:05.691 --> 00:03:12.897
"This place is strange," Perda commented as she and Zann paused in the doorway of a room that

58
00:03:12.937 --> 00:03:15.599
appeared to be made entirely out of fish scales.

59
00:03:15.619 --> 00:03:17.640
"Yeah," Zann said.

60
00:03:17.660 --> 00:03:19.361
"Just like the guy who built it."

61
00:03:19.381 --> 00:03:20.662
"Look out!"

62
00:03:20.923 --> 00:03:21.583
Venna cried.

63
00:03:22.304 --> 00:03:24.325
Several large trolls lumbered toward them.

64
00:03:24.345 --> 00:03:25.766
"Zing, quick!"

65
00:03:25.986 --> 00:03:26.607
Darb urged.

66
00:03:26.627 --> 00:03:27.828
"Do your thing!"

67
00:03:29.052 --> 00:03:31.353
Whistling his song, Zing flew forward.

68
00:03:31.973 --> 00:03:34.354
The trolls stopped, staring at the dragon.

69
00:03:34.374 --> 00:03:38.996
"Hurry! If we get out of sight, they might forget we were ever here.

70
00:03:39.016 --> 00:03:41.037
"Venna darted around a corner.

71
00:03:41.777 --> 00:03:45.099
By the time the group rounded the next corner, Zing had caught up.

72
00:03:45.919 --> 00:03:47.660
Zann didn't hear any sound of pursuit.

73
00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:50.601
"I think we lost them," he said.

74
00:03:50.621 --> 00:03:51.921
"Thanks, little buddy!"

75
00:03:53.002 --> 00:03:57.844
Zing chirped and led the way into a large courtyard filled with trees and shrubs.

76
00:03:58.708 --> 00:03:59.969
"Wow," Perda said.

77
00:03:59.989 --> 00:04:04.130
"This place is definitely bigger on the inside than the outside!"

78
00:04:04.150 --> 00:04:07.252
"Perhaps." Wyssa looked worried.

79
00:04:07.272 --> 00:04:11.013
"There might be a Bewilderment spell on the whole place.

80
00:04:11.853 --> 00:04:16.035
That would explain why we never pass the same room twice."

81
00:04:16.055 --> 00:04:18.496
"A Bewilderment spell?"

82
00:04:18.656 --> 00:04:19.136
Gliss said.

83
00:04:19.156 --> 00:04:21.437
"I've never heard of—aah!"

84
00:04:22.098 --> 00:04:23.078
Zann spun around.

85
00:04:23.358 --> 00:04:24.899
One of the trees had grabbed Gliss!

86
00:04:24.919 --> 00:04:27.080
"It's a tentacle tree!"

87
00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:27.840
Perda cried.

88
00:04:28.284 --> 00:04:29.405
"Like in Fardark!"

89
00:04:30.425 --> 00:04:31.386
Wyssa stepped forward.

90
00:04:31.746 --> 00:04:34.348
A long, curved knife appeared in her hand.

91
00:04:35.008 --> 00:04:38.530
With one swift movement, she slashed the tentacle in two.

92
00:04:38.550 --> 00:04:40.891
"Get away from it," she ordered.

93
00:04:40.911 --> 00:04:45.634
"Hurry!" The whole group dashed through another door.

94
00:04:45.654 --> 00:04:48.696
"This is awful!"

95
00:04:48.996 --> 00:04:50.397
Venna looked petrified.

96
00:04:50.417 --> 00:04:56.020
"It's like Morb brought every scary creature from every world to guard this place!"

97
00:04:56.788 --> 00:04:58.610
There was a sudden flurry of wings.

98
00:04:59.210 --> 00:05:01.872
Dozens of large birds burst into the room.

99
00:05:01.892 --> 00:05:03.834
"Snuffer geese!"

100
00:05:04.174 --> 00:05:04.955
Gliss exclaimed.

101
00:05:04.975 --> 00:05:06.756
"Or sniffer geese?

102
00:05:07.077 --> 00:05:09.579
I can't tell the difference."

103
00:05:09.599 --> 00:05:11.320
"Doesn't matter," Wyssa said.

104
00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:14.483
"Both breeds are nasty when they're annoyed."

105
00:05:15.203 --> 00:05:16.565
Darb took a deep breath.

106
00:05:16.585 --> 00:05:18.486
"Honk! Honk!"

107
00:05:18.506 --> 00:05:20.848
"What's your Void friend doing?"

108
00:05:20.968 --> 00:05:22.109
Venna hissed at Zann.

109
00:05:22.129 --> 00:05:23.931
"He'll only upset them more!"

110
00:05:23.951 --> 00:05:28.114
"Shh!" Zann watched as Darb honked a few more times.

111
00:05:28.955 --> 00:05:30.155
One of the geese honked back.

112
00:05:30.816 --> 00:05:33.097
Then the whole flock waddled off!

113
00:05:33.117 --> 00:05:36.240
"Amazing!" Gliss cried.

114
00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:38.001
They all looked at Darb.

115
00:05:38.641 --> 00:05:39.142
He shrugged.

116
00:05:39.162 --> 00:05:41.643
"I just told them we didn't mean them any harm.

117
00:05:42.004 --> 00:05:43.945
At least I think that's what I said!"

118
00:05:44.686 --> 00:05:45.706
Venna looked impressed.

119
00:05:46.767 --> 00:05:48.448
"Let's move on," said Wyssa.

120
00:05:49.329 --> 00:05:50.830
She led the way into the next room.

121
00:05:51.791 --> 00:05:53.532
It was large and dimly lit.

122
00:05:54.588 --> 00:05:59.572
As Zann entered the room, he thought he saw a shadowy shape moving along one wall.

123
00:06:00.352 --> 00:06:02.634
He paused and peered into the dimness.

124
00:06:02.654 --> 00:06:04.635
"Guys?" said Zann.

125
00:06:04.655 --> 00:06:07.017
"I think there's something in here."

126
00:06:07.797 --> 00:06:10.819
Just then the shadowy creature stepped into the light.

127
00:06:11.480 --> 00:06:13.801
The creature was orange with black stripes.

128
00:06:14.942 --> 00:06:15.663
Perda gasped.

129
00:06:16.023 --> 00:06:18.104
"It's one of those striped monsters.

130
00:06:18.865 --> 00:06:23.228
Like the one Morb sent after that sneaky guy, Slib, back at the palace!"

131
00:06:24.188 --> 00:06:26.069
"How do we fight this creature?"

132
00:06:26.229 --> 00:06:26.849
Gliss asked.

133
00:06:27.589 --> 00:06:28.269
Venna shrugged.

134
00:06:28.289 --> 00:06:33.951
"Run!" Zann was in the lead as they raced around a corner and straight into a flock of

135
00:06:34.071 --> 00:06:35.491
tiny, buzzing creatures.

136
00:06:35.511 --> 00:06:41.273
"Flizzes!" he shouted, steeling himself for the little dragons' painful stings.

137
00:06:41.993 --> 00:06:42.793
But it didn't happen.

138
00:06:43.113 --> 00:06:45.074
The flizzes immediately buzzed away.

139
00:06:45.094 --> 00:06:47.314
"Wow," Perda said.

140
00:06:47.334 --> 00:06:49.775
"We're lucky they didn't attack us."

141
00:06:49.795 --> 00:06:51.576
"Maybe not."

142
00:06:51.856 --> 00:06:52.876
Wyssa sounded grim.

143
00:06:53.612 --> 00:06:57.560
"They're probably flying straight to Morb to tell him that we're here."
